-- title:
--   First inequality for idele classes of a cyclic extension
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ an algebra over $K$ such that $L/K$ is Galois with cyclic Galois group $L \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K]} L$, and let $B$ be an adele base-change datum of type `AdeleBaseChange (𝓞 K) K (𝓞 L) L`, that is: a ring homomorphism $\beta \colon \mathbb{A}_K \to \mathbb{A}_L$ between the adele rings, commuting with the diagonal embeddings in the sense that $\beta(\iota_K(e)) = \iota_L(e)$ for every $e \in K$, together with an isomorphism of $\mathbb{A}_K$-algebras $\mathbb{A}_K \otimes_K L \cong \mathbb{A}_L$ (for the $\mathbb{A}_K$-algebra structure on $\mathbb{A}_L$ given by $\beta$) sending $1 \otimes f$ to $\iota_L(f)$ for every $f \in L$. Write $N$ for the induced map on units, namely the image under `Units.map` of the algebra norm $\mathbb{A}_L \to \mathbb{A}_K$ for that structure, and let $P \le \mathbb{A}_K^\times$ be the subgroup of principal ideles, the range of $K^\times \to \mathbb{A}_K^\times$. The conclusion is that the index of the subgroup generated by $P$ together with the image of $N$ is nonzero, i.e. that this subgroup has finite index in $\mathbb{A}_K^\times$, and that $[L:K] =$ `Module.finrank K L` divides this index.
--
--   This is the first inequality of global class field theory in idelic form: for a cyclic extension $L/K$ the norm coset index $[\mathbb{A}_K^\times : K^\times N_{L/K}(\mathbb{A}_L^\times)]$ is finite and divisible by $[L:K]$. It is taken up in the construction of first-inequality data for idele class groups and of Hecke-character input at a cyclic or prime-degree layer.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_M4aHerbrand_ideleClass_normCoset_index_ne_zero_and_finrank_dvd.lean

